    {
      "text": "This section presents an algorithm that uses bounded error methods for solving the inference problem in an arbitrary",
      "bbox": [
        46.48500061035156,
        285.14666748046875,
        500.0005187988281,
        294.2724304199219
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "graphical model. In fact, the use of interval representations offers many advantages, basically:",
      "bbox": [
        46.48500061035156,
        297.6029052734375,
        420.3714599609375,
        306.7286682128906
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "1. a reduction of the memory space required to store the messages and beliefs.",
      "bbox": [
        48.97764205932617,
        314.0461730957031,
        362.76800537109375,
        323.17193603515625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "2. energy saving since the exchanged information between communicating nodes is much less bulky (this also",
      "bbox": [
        48.97764205932617,
        326.5024108886719,
        500.0294189453125,
        335.628173828125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "implies a reduction of the required bandwidth).",
      "bbox": [
        61.43387985229492,
        338.9496765136719,
        249.3096923828125,
        348.075439453125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "3. using interval-based representations avoids the overhead associated with the computation of nonparametric",
      "bbox": [
        48.97764205932617,
        351.4059143066406,
        500.0408020019531,
        360.53167724609375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "density estimates and the procedure of sampling from the product of Gaussian mixtures in NBP. This translates",
      "bbox": [
        61.43387985229492,
        363.8621520996094,
        500.0584411621094,
        372.9879150390625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "into simpler and faster computations and thus more time saving (see Sect. 7).",
      "bbox": [
        61.43387985229492,
        376.3094177246094,
        368.2769775390625,
        385.4351806640625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "4. avoiding the need to introduce artiﬁcial parameters in order to approximate the true messages, since a set of",
      "bbox": [
        48.977630615234375,
        388.7656555175781,
        499.9994201660156,
        397.89141845703125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "boxes constitute a direct approximation of the pdf, and getting around the convergence problem of MCMC",
      "bbox": [
        61.433868408203125,
        401.2218933105469,
        500.02532958984375,
        410.34765625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "samplers.",
      "bbox": [
        61.433868408203125,
        413.6691589355469,
